PLAN=plan(4,'Fractions and decimals','Part I · The grammar of number',16,'Scientific and technical innovation','Equivalence, Representation','The same quantity can be written as a fraction, a decimal or a measurement; choosing a representation makes comparison and calculation more reliable.','A recipe must serve nine people instead of six. How can every ingredient change proportionally without changing the taste?','In order for a student to transfer mathematical knowledge, students must connect representations and apply a known method in a new measurement or recipe context.',S,explore,application,assessment,mixed,ready,check,[S[0]['diagram'],S[3]['diagram'],S[5]['diagram']],['Simplify and compare fractions.','Use all four operations with fractions and decimals.','Round with stated precision and convert representations.','Scale a recipe and justify exact versus rounded measurements.'],'numerator · denominator · equivalent · simplest form · common denominator · reciprocal · terminating · repeating · precision',sourcepages='74–94; answers 222–225')
